 ## Overview
-Customization Volume Integration is a method that integrates a pre-computed customization volume into the volume rendering pipeline to apply position-dependent modifications to visualization parameters, such as gamma correction of intensity values [S1]. Unlike global transfer function adjustments or standard ray casting [12643-standard-ray-casting.md], this method decouples the modification logic from the ray-casting loop's core compositing, allowing for complex, spatially coherent parameter fields (e.g., Voronoi-based seeds) to drive the visualization [S1].
+Customization Volume Integration is a method that integrates a pre-computed customization volume into the volume rendering pipeline to apply position-dependent modifications to visualization parameters, such as gamma correction of intensity values [S1]. It enables localized control over rendering appearance without altering the underlying scalar field [S1]. Unlike global transfer function adjustments, this approach decouples the modification logic from the core compositing loop, allowing spatially coherent parameter fields to drive the visualization [S1].
 
